WineD3D island p70: route only ABI-admitted draw-state phase A.

The p69 whole context_apply_draw_state() boundary rendered black and the
transitive shared-heap audit explains why it was not an admissible root:
glsl_ffp_fragment_shader is 164 bytes in guest i386 and 132 bytes in ARM.
Keep the guest as owner of context_apply_draw_state(), dirty-state application,
bindings/FBO and the ABI-unsafe shader backend.  Move only the contiguous
resource/stream preload transaction into entry 40, including stream-info and
index-buffer maintenance.

This patch restores draw_primitive() to the direct guest
context_apply_draw_state() call added around by patch 66; entry 39 remains only
as a rejected historical symbol and is not armed.  The phase comments are
analysis boundaries, not runtime selectors.

The independent indirect-call audit found nine remaining callbacks reachable
from the conservative phase-A closure. Route them through the existing class
A/B/C dispatch families; the final p70 audit reports zero unrouted calls.  The
transitive ABI admission matrix reports entry 10/23/38 PASS, p69/D FAIL, and
phase A PASS with 1,096 TU-qualified aggregate rows, zero mismatches and zero
hard failures.

The first run is correctness-only.  It makes no frame-rate claim.

